@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo, AND THAT IS CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P17-QUAL-001 FULL P17 QUALIFICATION. The exact invocation, recorded so
rem the run is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, THIRTY-ONE in a row counting this one.
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem
rem CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6, carried for the reason INFRA-VIEWER-001
rem recorded: 16 logical cores let `cmake --build` run 18 compiles at once, and
rem a CLEAN build of over 600 template-heavy translation units exhausted the
rem commit charge. Capping parallelism weakens nothing -- same sources, same
rem flags, -Werror included. ctest stays at -j 8.
rem
rem WHAT THIS MILESTONE ADDS, and it is the same shape as P16-QUAL-001: one
rem test file holding the final cross-milestone gates, its registration, one
rem more zero-match filter, and NO production change.
rem
rem   NEW          tests/qualification/P17StructuralQualificationTests.cpp
rem                              3 cases: solving leaves every reference
rem                              document byte-identical; every dependency
rem                              edit stales the result in one sequence with
rem                              undo in the middle; a FAILED regeneration
rem                              never yields a current result
rem   MODIFIED     tests/CMakeLists.txt                    1 source
rem                tests/cli/ZeroMatchGuard.cmake          1 filter,
rem                                                        unit\.P17Qualification 3
rem
rem NOT ONE FILE under src/, include/, apps/ or examples/ changed. The ADR
rem amendments, ARCHITECTURE.md and the P17-VIZ-001 addenda are under docs/,
rem outside the eight-path fingerprint by construction.
rem
rem SEVEN MUTATION PROBES were run on the production tree before this launch
rem and every file was restored (git status recorded in MUTATION.md); the
rem harness then cleans and rebuilds every preset from the restored tree, so
rem no probe binary can be the one that runs here.
rem
rem What IS in the repeat set, and why. THE FILTER IS UNCHANGED from
rem P17-REFMOD-001: the new cases are named unit.P17Qualification*, and
rem `unit\.P17Qualification` is added to the filter below so the final gates
rem are repeated five times as well. The SELECTED COUNT IS RECORDED BY THIS
rem RUN rather than predicted here.
rem
rem compile_fail is excluded from the REPEAT for the reason the previous
rem milestones recorded: each case is a real COMPILATION, so repeating one
rem measures the compiler's determinism and not BetterCAD's. They still run
rem UNFILTERED in all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem
rem THIS RUN HAPPENS ON THE HASIB MACHINE, as P17-CLI-001's and
rem P17-REFMOD-001's did, by the owner's decision of 2026-10-14. What is
rem identical to the uqhas machine, checked rather than assumed: GCC 16.1.0
rem WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4, the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it bundles, and the
rem dependency prefix built by deps/CMakeLists.txt from the same hash-verified
rem archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen 6.2.2604.
rem
rem What differs, and why each is in the CACHE rather than on this line:
rem   BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT        C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build, below
rem   BETTERCAD_DEPS_PREFIX       C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bettercad-deps/
rem                               gnu-16-mingw-amd64. The %LOCALAPPDATA%
rem                               default could not be used: a shell launched
rem                               from the packaged Claude desktop app has its
rem                               AppData\Local writes virtualised into the
rem                               app's container, which Qt's build-path check
rem                               refuses and no other shell can see.
rem   FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_*   Catch2, nlohmann_json and Eigen from
rem                               archives fetched outside CMake and verified
rem                               against the SHA256 in
rem                               cmake/BetterCADDependencies.cmake, because
rem                               the bundled CMake's curl has no CA trust
rem                               anchors (carried constraint 7).
rem Each tree was configured with those three -D flags for P17-CLI-001;
rem qualify.cmd's plain `cmake --preset` reuses the cache.
setlocal
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/Users/hasib/bcdev/bc-build"
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=6"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Structural|unit\.P17Qualification|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.structural\."
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
